# Task 143-011: Rule Generator (3 Provider)

## Approach
1. Create `src/core/rule-generator.ts` — template engine that:
   - Reads ADR entries from MemoryStore
   - Renders 3 role templates (brain, auditor, worker-default) 
   - Outputs to 3 provider directories (.claude/rules/, .codex/rules/, .gemini/rules/)
   - Preserves user custom sections via <!-- CUSTOM-START/END --> markers

2. Create 3 template files in `src/core/rule-templates/`:
   - brain.template.md
   - auditor.template.md  
   - worker-default.template.md

3. Create 3 provider adapters in `src/core/rule-generator.ts` (inline):
   - Claude: frontmatter with `paths:` field
   - Codex: Codex instruction format
   - Gemini: Gemini rules format

4. Wire `regenerateRules()` into sprint-finalizer via existing `onRuleRegen` hook

5. Write 15+ tests in `tests/core/rule-generator.test.ts`

## Files to Create
- src/core/rule-generator.ts (main module)
- src/core/rule-templates/brain.template.md
- src/core/rule-templates/auditor.template.md
- src/core/rule-templates/worker-default.template.md
- tests/core/rule-generator.test.ts
- .codex/rules/brain.md
- .codex/rules/auditor.md
- .codex/rules/worker-default.md
- .gemini/rules/brain.md
- .gemini/rules/auditor.md
- .gemini/rules/worker-default.md

## Files to Modify
- src/orchestra/sprint-finalizer.ts (wire onRuleRegen)
- src/core/identity-generator.ts (if needed for hook)

## Key Design Decisions
- Templates stored as .template.md files, read at runtime via fs
- Provider adapters are functions, not classes (KISS)
- AUTO/CUSTOM section markers preserve user edits
- Idempotent: running twice produces same output
